# THE WAY UP, SEEN BEFORE IT IS TAKEN (43_climb `_show_cable`, #32): the cable
# that hangs from the lame walker's drum into its middle toe's crater, from the
# lip, coming down over it, and at its foot. One round rope lit its whole length,
# two dark strands laid round it, a band at every ledge and the longest at its
# foot on the crater floor: by day one line, by night the line the eye goes to.
# Shoot it at dusk and night too by passing the hour (`--hour=20.4`, `--hour=23`,
# with the rest of the run line, which the command line then replaces).
#   TOUR_TIMEOUT=900 tools/tour.sh tours/climb-cable.tour --seed=1 --place=tread0 --colossus=2@tread0+5 --hour=12 --weather=clear:0
at climb:lip
zoom 30
shot 00-from-the-lip-zoomed-out-the-rope-hangs-into-the-crater with colossus_tread,climb_patch,climb_foot_seen
zoom 15
wait 2.0
walkto at:climb:cable 60 till:climb_foot_seen
shot 01-over-the-lip-the-rope-comes-into-view with colossus_tread,climb_patch,climb_foot_seen
walkto at:climb:cable 60
# The walk stops WALK_NAMED_NEAR (3 tiles) short; the frame wants him beside the foot.
at climb:cable
back here 1.2
wait 1.0
shot 02-at-the-foot-the-rope-and-its-lit-band with colossus_tread,climb_cable,climb_patch
